the National Rifle Association has filed  a lawsuit to try to block a Florida  School Safety bill that puts new  restrictions on guns final passage of  the measure came after a gunman killed  17 people at a high school with a  semi-automatic assault style rifle last  month Florida's governor says the bill  balances individual rights with the need  for Public Safety Adriana Diaz reports  with the sweep of a pen Florida Governor  Rick Scott is allowing some teachers to  carry guns in classrooms while also  tightening access to firearms the new  law also limits rifle sales to people 21  or over after a three day waiting period  allows law enforcement to confiscate  firearms from people who make threats  and allocates four hundred million  dollars for school safety and mental  health but what it doesn't do is ban  assault rifles the one thing that the  students had a consensus on is that they  wanted an assault weapons ban this bill  doesn't this law doesn't include that  rather than banning specific weapons we  need to ban specific people from having  any weapon by allowing some school staff  to carry weapons in counties that opt  into the program Florida joins at least  11 other states with similar measures  but teachers in Florida's Union  including Felicia Alvarez and Shane cook  want guns out of schools  these students are our future right now  we are showing them that the answer to  violence is more violence the idea of  being armed is very enticing but the  bigger issue is that we're creating laws  that are not fixing the problem the  families of all 17 victims in the  Parkland shootings support the new law  some like tonymont Aalto who lost his  daughter Gina were there for the signing  we have paid a terrible price for this  progress we call on more states to  follow Florida's lead and create  meaningful legislation to make all  schools safer this time must be  different gun control laws have emerged  from other school shootings but what's  significant about this state is that  Florida is such a gun friendly state it  also has a republic  governor and republican-controlled  legislature now governor Scott is a  member of the NRA  he received an A+ rating from the NRA  but he broke from the NRA with this move  earlier this week an NRA lobbyist said  that the legislation was a display of  quote bullying and coercion for CBS this  morning Saturday Adriana Diaz  Tallahassee
 

